hs of righteousness for his name\u2019s sake. Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil: for thou art with me; thy rod and thy staff they comfort me. Thou preparest a table before me in the presence of mine enemies: thou anointest my head with oil; my cup runneth over. Surely goodness and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life: and I will dwell in the house of the Lord for ever.\nPsalm 23, King James Version","align":"c","ls":1.3,"font":"LA","size":10.2,"color":"#2C3650","spc":0.0,"prose":{"font":"LA","size":10.2,"color":"#2C3650","ls":1.3,"after":6.12},"poem":{"font":"LAi","size":9.6,"color":"#2C3650","ls":1.18,"stanza":5.28},"source":{"font":"LAi","size":8,"color":"#5F6882","ls":1.0,"before":5.6}},{"t":"text","bind":"in_memory","x":0.38,"y":4.78,"w":3.24,"h":0.1562,"anchor":"m","sample":"In loving memory of","align":"c","ls":1.0,"font":"LAi","size":9.0,"color":"#5F6882","spc":0.0},{"t":"text","bind":"name","x":0.38,"y":4.9562,"w":3.24,"h":0.2456,"anchor":"m","sample":"Eleanor Grace Whitfield","align":"c","ls":0.95,"font":"PF","size":13.0,"color":"#1E2A44","spc":0.0},{"t":"text","bind":"dates","x":0.38,"y":5.2218,"w":3.24,"h":0.1892,"anchor":"m","sample":"March 4, 1941 \u2013 September 12, 2026","align":"c","ls":1.1,"font":"LA","size":8.6,"color":"#2C3650","spc":0.2}],"bg":"cm-bg-prayer-46-navy-back.jpg","px":[1200,1800]}],"sage":[{"design":"sage","side":"front","w":4.0,"h":6.0,"els":[{"t":"text","bind":"kicker","x":0.2,"y":0.36,"w":3.6,"h":0.62,"anchor":"m","sample":"Celebration of Life","align":"c","ls":1.0,"font":"GV","size":27.44,"color":"#5A7A62","spc":0.0},{"t":"photo","bind":"photo","x":0.85,"y":1.06,"w":2.3,"h":2.8111,"border":"#86A382","bw":1.0},{"t":"text","bind":"name","x":0.35,"y":4.0111,"w":3.3,"h":0.62,"anchor":"m","sample":"Eleanor Grace Whitfield","align":"c","ls":0.92,"font":"PF","size":19.0,"color":"#2F4034","spc":0.0},{"t":"text","bind":"dates","x":0.35,"y":4.6911,"w":3.3,"h":0.21,"anchor":"m","sample":"March 4, 1941 \u2013 September 12, 2026","align":"c","ls":1.15,"font":"LA","size":9.5,"color":"#33403A","spc":0.2}],"bg":"cm-bg-prayer-46-sage-front.jpg","px":[1200,1800]},{"design":"sage","side":"back","w":4.0,"h":6.0,"els":[{"t":"text","bind":"verse_title","x":0.2,"y":0.76,"w":3.6,"h":0.36,"anchor":"m","sample":"Crossing the Bar","align":"c","ls":1.0,"font":"PF","size":15.0,"color":"#51705A","spc":0.0},{"t":"verse","bind":"verse","x":0.38,"y":1.18,"w":3.24,"h":3.5,"anchor":"m","sample":"Sunset and evening star,\nAnd one clear call for me!\nAnd may there be no moaning of the bar,\nWhen I put out to sea,\nBut such a tide as moving seems asleep,\nToo full for sound and foam,\nWhen that which drew from out the boundless deep\nTurns again home.\nTwilight and evening bell,\nAnd after that the dark!\nAnd may there be no sadness of farewell,\nWhen I embark;\nFor tho\u2019 from out our bourne of Time and Place\nThe flood may bear me far,\nI hope to see my Pilot face to face\nWhen I have crost the bar.\nAlfred, Lord Tennyson","align":"c","ls":1.18,"font":"LAi","size":9.6,"color":"#33403A","spc":0.0,"prose":{"font":"LA","size":10.2,"color":"#33403A","ls":1.3,"after":6.12},"poem":{"font":"LAi","size":9.6,"color":"#33403A","ls":1.18,"stanza":5.28},"source":{"font":"LAi","size":8,"color":"#66776B","ls":1.0,"before":5.6}},{"t":"text","bind":"in_memory","x":0.38,"y":4.78,"w":3.24,"h":0.1562,"anchor":"m","sample":"In loving memory of","align":"c","ls":1.0,"font":"LAi","size":9.0,"color":"#66776B","spc":0.0},{"t":"text","bind":"name","x":0.38,"y":4.9562,"w":3.24,"h":0.2456,"anchor":"m","sample":"Eleanor Grace Whitfield","align":"c","ls":0.95,"font":"PF","size":13.0,"color":"#2F4034","spc":0.0},{"t":"text","bind":"dates","x":0.38,"y":5.2218,"w":3.24,"h":0.1892,"anchor":"m","sample":"March 4, 1941 \u2013 September 12, 2026","align":"c","ls":1.1,"font":"LA","size":8.6,"color":"#33403A","spc":0.2}],"bg":"cm-bg-prayer-46-sage-back.jpg","px":[1200,1800]}],"rose":[{"design":"rose","si